# Working files, rewritten every run.
#
# Durable state, committed:
#   pool.jsonl   the candidate corpus, with per-paper `reviewed` state
#   seen.json    every id ever fetched — permanent, so pruning cannot resurrect
#   queue.jsonl  what to post, and what was posted
#
# batch.json is one review run's selection; drafts.json is what the agent
# proposed before the gate looked at it. Committing either would put a rejected
# draft in the history as though it had been approved.
batch.json
drafts.json
inbox.json
